---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="Colophon | Darren Haryanto">
  <section class="mb-16">
    <a
      href="/#content"
      class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-muted hover:text-accent transition-colors mb-10"
    >
      <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path>
      </svg>
      Back to portfolio
    </a>

    <h1 class="text-primary font-display font-medium text-5xl md:text-6xl tracking-tight mb-4">
      Colophon<span class="text-accent">.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed text-lg max-w-2xl">
      The making of this site: what it runs on, the type it's set in, and the things I tried
      that didn't survive.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-16 pb-12 border-b border-border max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="text-primary font-bold mb-6 uppercase tracking-wider text-sm">Stack</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4 text-muted leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        This is a static <a href="https://astro.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-accent hover:underline">Astro</a>
        site styled with Tailwind CSS v4. There's no client framework; the interactive parts,
        the theme toggle, the lightbox, the pointer effects, are small hand-written scripts.
        Every project page is generated from one typed data file, so adding a project means
        editing code, not a CMS.
      </p>
      <p>
        It's deployed on my own server with Docker Compose behind nginx. The code lives on
        GitHub and on a self-hosted Gitea instance, where a workflow checks the production
        build on every push.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-16 pb-12 border-b border-border max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="text-primary font-bold mb-6 uppercase tracking-wider text-sm">Type &amp; color</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4 text-muted leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Headings are set in <span class="text-primary font-display">Fraunces</span>, a serif with
        enough character to not feel like a template. Body text is Inter Tight, and the small
        labels, dates, and tags are <span class="font-mono text-sm">JetBrains Mono</span>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Colors are defined in OKLCH around a single blue accent. Dark is the default; the light
        theme flips with a circular reveal that spreads out from the toggle button, driven by the
        View Transitions API. A faint film grain sits over everything so the flat surfaces read
        as paper rather than plastic.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-16 pb-12 border-b border-border max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="text-primary font-bold mb-6 uppercase tracking-wider text-sm">What didn't survive</h2>
    <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed mb-6">
      The git history remembers everything I changed my mind about. A few of them:
    </p>
    <ul class="space-y-4 text-muted leading-relaxed">
      <li class="pl-6 border-l-2 border-border">
        The project cards used to tilt about four degrees toward the pointer. It looked like the
        cards were being dragged around the page, so the tilt is now 1.5 degrees, barely there
        on purpose.
      </li>
      <li class="pl-6 border-l-2 border-border">
        My phone number sat in the hero next to Email and LinkedIn. It's a GitHub link now,
        which is more useful to anyone actually reading this page.
      </li>
      <li class="pl-6 border-l-2 border-border">
        The first screenshot gallery was a tall masonry wall that pushed the write-ups below the
        fold. It became a compact filmstrip instead.
      </li>
      <li class="pl-6 border-l-2 border-border">
        A "Scroll to explore" prompt is still in the source, commented out. The hero fading as
        you scroll turned out to explain itself.
      </li>
      <li class="pl-6 border-l-2 border-border">
        At one point I went through the copy and removed every em dash.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="text-primary font-bold mb-6 uppercase tracking-wider text-sm">Small print</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4 text-muted leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        The doodles in the hero are hand-tweaked SVG paths that draw themselves, hold for a
        moment, and erase on a loop. Most of them are hidden on phones.
      </p>
      <p>
        The cursor ring, the glow that pools over the content, and the magnetic buttons in the
        corner are deliberately faint, and all of them switch off on touch screens and under
        <span class="font-mono text-sm">prefers-reduced-motion</span>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The timestamp in the footer is the date of the last commit, read from git when the
        site builds.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
